    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_f443062911b688ab78961868f28afa9f28f14a9fac4c7baa0ba57d4d660ffe35",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The Selberg class calculation and the abstract flow calculation generate orbit weights by localization. Diagonalizing a hyperbolic representative and integrating over its centralizer strip leaves primitive length, repetition, and a hyperbolic-sine stability factor; pulling a flow-graph distribution back to the diagonal and pushing it to time yields primitive-period covolume divided by the determinant of one minus the transverse return map. Thus the coefficients arise from quotient and restriction Jacobians rather than being appended after a spectral match.",
